    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Long and short vowels",
     "texto": [
      "In a stressed syllable, the vowel can be long or short. As a rough guide, a vowel before a single consonant is usually long; before a double consonant or a consonant group it is usually short. There are exceptions.",
      "Length can change the meaning: **vin** («wine») and **vinn** («wins»). The written double consonant usually shows a short vowel."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
